WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  dalian atkinson was a star footballer  best known for his time at aston villa  he was 48 when he died  soon after being tasered and kicked in  the head by a police officer  pc benjamin monk is now on trial for  murder  his west mercier police colleague pc  mary ellen betley smith  on trial for assault they were called by  neighbors who'd heard mr atkinson  shouting outside his father's house in  telford  in the early hours in august 2016.  mr atkinson was unarmed but his behavior  was erratic  and he was claiming to be the messiah pc  monk fired his taser  three times twice it didn't work but the  third time  dalian atkinson fell forwards onto the  road  the prosecutor told the jury the  standard default setting of a taser is a  five-second phase  but it's possible to override that by  continuing to depress the trigger  pc monk continued to depress the trigger  for over six  times the length of a standard phase the  taser was deployed  for 33 seconds the court heard that  neighbours who were watching said once  dalian atkinson was on the ground he was  unresponsive and still  so no longer a threat to the officers  but they continued  pc betley smith struck him several times  with a bat  on and pc monk kicked him in the head at  least twice  so hard he left the imprint of his  shoelaces  on his forehead dalian atkinson died in  hospital  a short time later both pc monk  and pc betley smith deny all the charges  against them  their defense cases will be made in the  coming weeks  at the time of his death mr atkinson had  been suffering with serious health  conditions  including heart disease and end stage  renal failure  but the prosecution say their medical  experts believe were it not for the  taser deployment and kicks to his head  he would not have died that night becky  johnson  sky news birmingham

